# Development Handoff Summary

When asked for a handoff, produce:

- **Implemented** — what works now, by module (`MOD-xx`) and app (`server`/`frontend`/`app`).
- **Files modified/created** — grouped by app, with one-line purpose each.
- **Architecture touched** — engines, schemas, routes, slices affected; any new patterns introduced.
- **Decisions** — technical choices made and why; link the ADR or spec section (`docs/platform/..`).
- **Spec updates** — which docs in `docs/platform/` were changed (or still need changing) to match the code.
- **Remaining tasks** — ordered, with acceptance references (`BR-xx-nn`, endpoint, screen).
- **Known issues / risks** — bugs, flaky tests, TODOs, security follow-ups.
- **Verification** — exact commands run (`npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `prisma validate`, …) and their results.

Make it detailed enough that a fresh agent conversation can continue the work without repeating the investigation.
